        {''.join(f'<tr><td>{dec}s</td><td>{fmt_num(a["decades"][dec]["total_volume"])}</td><td>{fmt_num(int(a["decades"][dec]["total_volume"] / max(1, a["decades"][dec]["trading_days"])))}</td><td>—</td></tr>' for dec in sorted(a['decades'].keys()))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- SECTION 5: DIVIDEND HISTORY & STOCK SPLITS -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<section id="dividends-splits">
  <h2>Dividend History & Stock Splits</h2>
  <div class="section-obj">Documentation of the history of dividend payments and stock splits, dividend yield trends over time, and assessment of AXP's income-generation profile for long-term shareholders.</div>

  <div class="chart-box">
    <canvas id="chartDividends"></canvas>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-box">
    <canvas id="chartDivYield"></canvas>
  </div>

  <div class="narrative">
    <p>American Express has maintained a consistent dividend program throughout its history. The cumulative dividends paid per share total <strong>${kpi['total_dividends_per_share']:.2f}</strong>, which, while meaningful, represents only about <strong>{(kpi['total_dividends_per_share'] / kpi['end_price'] * 100):.1f}%</strong> of the current share price. This underscores AXP's character as primarily a growth stock rather than an income vehicle — the vast majority of total shareholder return has come from capital appreciation.</p>

    <p>Dividend payments have grown substantially over time, particularly in the post-2010 era as AXP's profitability improved and management committed to returning capital to shareholders. The dividend yield has typically ranged between <strong>0.5% and 2.5%</strong> depending on prevailing stock prices, placing AXP in the moderate-yield category among financial stocks.</p>

    {f'<p>The dataset records <strong>{len([e for e in a["dividend_events"] if e["amount"] > 0])}</strong> individual dividend payment events and <strong>{len(a["split_events"])}</strong> stock split events, reflecting AXP\'s corporate actions over the decades.</p>' if a['split_events'] else ''}
  </div>

  <h3>Dividend Yield History (2000–2026)</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Total Dividends/Share ($)</th><th>Avg Close Price ($)</th><th>Dividend Yield (%)</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{div_yield_rows}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  {f'''<h3>Stock Split History</h3>
